I cut "groundbreaking," "plagued users," "seamlessly," and "robust and comprehensive" because none of them tell a reviewer anything they can check. I also replaced "completely resolves" and "all tool-result scenarios" because a PR shouldn't claim full coverage unless it lists what was tested.

The description would be stronger with facts I couldn't find in the text:
- the decoder's real name or file path;
- the issue number this fixes;
- the tests added, such as which block types and tool-result shapes they cover;
- any block types the decoder still doesn't handle.

